WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.610
Well then,

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:04.230
since all of you have gotten your coins...

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.240
I will explain the rules for the second preliminary.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:13.240
This time, all of the ingredients that are
on the coins which you have acquired...

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.330
<i>must</i> be used to make a single bread.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.790
If there is even a single unused ingredient...

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.470
You will be immediately disqualified.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:24.960
All of the ingredients?

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:29.000
Farewell, Japanese representative.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.390
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.310
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:37.600
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.050
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:46.190
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.830
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:23.420
<i>Lupan</i> #3!!

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.140
Pain d’épice, Kai-style(Kai)!

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:38.730
Kawachi!

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:40.510
Where are you going?

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.640
Kuro-yan, what the hell does this mean?!

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:47.410
If there was such a rule last year,
why didn’t you tell us?

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:50.330
If that was the case,
like the French representatives,

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:52.520
we’d have paid attention to
the number of ingredients we got.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:55.000
Calm down, Kawachi.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.170
Ryou and I are both surprised as well.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:59.500
It’s a completely different rule from last year.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:00.630
What was that?!

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:02.320
If that’s so,

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:05.830
why did the French representative
hold back on getting coins?

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.970
I don’t like to say such things based on a mere guess...

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:12.330
but it could be that the rules had
been leaked to them beforehand.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.060
What was that?!

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.000
Don’t tell me that Pierrot was unjust...?

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.230
No.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.730
Pierrot’s merely the master of ceremonies and judge.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:22.760
He isn’t told about the rules until the day of the match.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.770
The rules are decided by the
Management Board of the Monaco Cup.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:32.770
A great deal of money, close to a
trillion yen, is involved in this match.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:38.620
They can’t afford to let the home team, which has
the most popularity, lose in the preliminaries.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:41.160
So, it’s not strange to have that level of shady activity.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:42.750
What was that?!

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.630
But, it’s a competition at the world level. That can’t...

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.620
That’s one “What was that?!” too many.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:50.620
It’s starting to get annoying, okay?

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:52.260
Suwabara...

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:53.390
Don’t worry.

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:57.520
I won’t lose to people who do things
that shame a samurai’s code of chivalry.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.560
Return to the competition hall immediately.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:04.140
We’ll get absolutely nothing out of it if we’re disqualified for being in the audience.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.170
295...

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:09.600
296...

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:12.200
Umm...

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:16.310
I just did a quick count, and
there are about 300 of these coins.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.710
300!

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:21.210
If we make a single bread...

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:23.340
using all of these many ingredients...

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:27.820
We can’t make anything but a
crappy bread that tastes awful, huh?

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:31.430
Look carefully, Kawachi.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:35.350
It’s not like each and every one of
them has a different ingredient on it.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:36.920
There are plenty that are multiples.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:40.920
That’s true.

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:42.490
Look.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:46.820
The number of coins may have been large, but actually, we have only 34 ingredients.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:48.150
We can work it out somehow.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:50.930
34 ingredients?!

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.320
You know...

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:57.580
Now may not be the time to tell you something like this,

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:01.040
but you can only make
bread with about ten ingredients.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:03.380
Any more is beyond imagination.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:05.610
Will you be unsatisfied if it’s not a <i>Japan</i>?

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:06.740
Huh?

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:07.800
How about you, Azuma?

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:08.880
What?

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.250
Like I care about something like that.

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:12.930
Like I said...

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:14.210
I won’t do anything.

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.310
In the next preliminary, between Japan and France.

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:20.520
A bet where the side with fewer points will leave.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.880
I accept that bet.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:24.850
If there’s only one of you,
then there shall only be one of us.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:26.470
I’ll take you on by myself.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:27.900
I...

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.930
really won’t do anything.

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:32.410
I’m grateful.

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:36.990
When I said “I wouldn’t do anything,”
I meant that I wouldn’t relax,

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:38.480
nor would I get worried.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:40.980
But...

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:43.610
I believe in you, Suwabara.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.330
I guess it’s time to lift the veil, then.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:50.080
From what?

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:55.330
I, Suwabara Kai, will exhibit a new style of bread.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:06.860
You have so many ingredients that you can’t carry them without placing them in a box.

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:10.190
Yet, you ignore the fact that
you can’t make a delicious bread

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:11.930
and refuse to give up on the challenge...

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:14.030
As expected of the Japanese.

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:16.440
Just like a kamikaze.

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.700
In that case,

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:20.290
I will give you the finishing blow.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:22.750
With my Archbishop’s hat...

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:25.050
The Kouglof au Miel.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:29.170
After using dirty little tricks...

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:33.600
There’s a Japanese saying:
“The chickens will come home to roost.”

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:36.230
The only one who’ll die...

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:39.120
is you!

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:41.040
What was that?!

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.050
At that time,

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:44.480
I was beaten by Azuma in the newcomers’ battle,

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:46.480
and even drew with Kawachi.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:47.600
I went completely berserk.

00:06:58.410 --> 00:06:59.230
Kai.

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:00.450
Master!

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:02.120
You have fallen low indeed

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:05.240
if you take your anger out on the dojo
after having lost in your bread competition.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:08.240
And for God’s sake, please stop. Seriously.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.500
I’m sorry to have shown you something so shameful.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:13.740
But, I... I...

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:14.970
Kai,

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:19.120
do you not know why you could not
win against that man called Azuma?

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:20.870
I do not know.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:24.090
That is because you do not have <i>Japan</i>.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:27.850
If you speak in terms of
“the way of the sword,”

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:32.270
the man called Azuma is the
founder of the “<i>Japan</i>-style” school.

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:33.980
In other words, he is a genius.

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:36.700
If you challenge him in the usual
manner, you cannot compare to him.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:40.190
Then, what can I do?

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:42.280
You must steal techniques.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:43.580
How can you...?!

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:45.460
Stealing is cowardly!

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:48.200
You <i>fool</i>!

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:54.410
Even <i>your</i> sword technique
consists of skills stolen from me, right?

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:56.540
Th-That is...

00:07:57.220 --> 00:07:59.470
Even the famous Yagyuu Muneyoshi

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:04.540
Was defeated by Kamizumi Nobotsuna
of the Shinkage school at the age of 38.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.310
Yagyuu became his disciple,

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:10.550
stole those skills, and then became the
founder of the Yagyuu Shinkage school.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:13.260
There is nothing shameful about stealing techniques!

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:16.230
Listen carefully, Kai.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:18.360
The history of bread is older than that of the sword.

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:20.030
It is most likely around 4000 years old.

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:23.020
It is probably not possible to make
an absolutely new bread anymore.

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:25.290
Even Azuma the genius

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:29.120
steals from various breads,
cakes, and the dietary culture of Japan,

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:32.030
improving them to make his <i>Japan</i>.

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.750
In that case, Kai,

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:35.550
you must steal the world’s breads and cakes...

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:38.280
No, steal the skills from
every culinary item in the world!

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.680
You must travel all over the world

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:43.260
and create it with your stolen techniques!

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:44.250
The <i>Lupan</i>!

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:52.600
The appearance of a new style of bread,

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:54.510
and its name is... <i>Lupan</i>!

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:56.010
Lupan
and its name is... <i>Lupan</i>!

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:57.920
<i>L-Lupan</i>, he says...

00:08:57.920 --> 00:08:59.440
That’s a weird name.

00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:00.820
<i>Lupan</i>...

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:02.530
When you say <i>Lupan</i>, you mean...?

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:03.750
No!

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:06.660
That isn’t it at all.

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:10.280
Either way, even though I was in Japan, I’ve stolen techniques from all over the world.

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:14.280
After research and reform,
I have completed up to <i>Lupan</i> #5.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:17.000
Just watch, Man in the Mask...

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.500
My <i>Lupan</i> #3, which will lure you to Hell!

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:26.310
Suwabara Kai’s pain d’épice (Kai)!

00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:33.980
I see...

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:35.730
That’s a possibility.

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:36.980
Pain d’épice.

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:39.220
It refers to a spicy bread in French.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:42.200
It might be the only bread in the world

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:44.480
that you can make with a large number of ingredients.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:51.040
I got a little scared when he
crushed the apple with his bare hand...

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:52.540
but with just that,

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:56.490
you can’t win against my Kouglof au Miel.

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:18.190
Pain d’épice is similar to curry.

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:19.050
Curry?

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:22.150
A large number of spices are used in curries,

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:25.030
and by including sweet
ingredients such as apples and honey,

00:10:25.030 --> 00:10:26.810
you can bring out a deep and good flavor.

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:28.780
I see.

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:32.160
So, in other words, since the pain d’épice uses spices,

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:34.210
even after using that many ingredients,

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:37.510
you can bring out a deep flavor like that of curry?

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:40.870
However, most likely...

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:43.420
Getting a high score will be really hard.

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:44.340
Yeah.

00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:47.220
Even if it is pain d’épice,

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:49.140
if you don’t apply some kind of trick to it,

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:52.080
you can’t use all 34 ingredients.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:55.310
Getting a high score like 4 or 5 points

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:58.590
will depend on the “Kai” factor, Suwabara-san.

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:10.330
Suwabara seems to be taking a lot of time...

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:12.870
I really think that it might be a good idea to help him.

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:15.000
We can’t. We promised not to.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.900
This time, we’ll leave it to him.

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:29.290
I’ve already finished baking it.

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:33.350
Oh well, it doesn’t matter how
long you take to make yours.

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:37.760
Please, just spare us an
ending where you say “I can’t do it.”

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:46.640
90% of the countries seem to have finished baking.

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:50.140
Japan still seems to be making theirs.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:54.330
Oh well, if he’s making it like that,
it’s going to take time.

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:03.090
The Pierrots have multiplied!

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:04.910
So, he’s already doing the scoring?!

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:07.720
I’ll start the scoring, but don’t worry.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:11.060
The preliminary does not really
require you to compete over time used.

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:14.920
Also, the kinds of ingredients
used vary from country to country.

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:19.000
So, the countries that have not yet
finished may continue with their work.

00:12:21.350 --> 00:12:24.480
However, though I may have cloned myself,

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:27.030
I still only have one stomach.

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:30.310
You can assume that those who finish late,
when I’m already full, are at a disadvantage.

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:32.810
This is really bad!

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:34.570
I’ll help him!

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.950
Don’t worry.

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:38.910
Azuma...

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:39.660
He’ll win...

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:40.610
Suwabara will.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.610
So, don’t interfere.

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:46.320
Canadian team gets 3 points.

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:49.800
Russian team is disqualified!

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:51.220
Wh-Why?!

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:54.040
You haven’t even eaten it,
so disqualifying us is...

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:56.420
This may be repetitive, but...

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:58.500
It’s because I’m Pierrot!

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:00.180
Kremlin!!

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:02.850
Once you become a world-level clown,

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:05.940
you will have a sense of smell that
allows you to distinguish the perfumes

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:08.390
of each person in a crowd of 10,000.

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:13.450
Your piroshki do not have the
cocoa you were required to add, right?

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:14.390
Wait one moment!

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:17.620
In that case, we can’t accept it. Khrushchev!

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:22.540
Yeah, it’s just a little, but
we’ve added cocoa. Andropov!

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:25.900
It’s not like we haven’t added
any at all. Battleship Potemkin!

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:28.340
That’s why you have been disqualified.

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:30.500
You really do not understand
what the problem is, do you?

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:33.970
Simply adding cocoa for the sake of adding it...

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:36.500
Your way of thinking is naive
and insufficient, just like the cocoa.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:41.380
I absolutely... hate... such cheaters.

00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:44.380
Sinful priest, Rasputin...

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:45.520
All right.

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:47.630
Since we’re done with the
scum, let us move on to France.

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:52.100
He’s beginning to score France.

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:54.060
Okay, 5 points, full score.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:56.490
Just wait one moment.

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:58.290
You just passed him by!

00:13:58.290 --> 00:14:00.540
Old... Mister Pierrot!

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:02.820
You haven’t even eaten it, so why is it a full score?

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:05.360
Because I ate it last year!

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:11.210
I have eaten his Kouglof au Miel at last year’s finals.

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:13.370
There’s no need to eat it once more.

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:15.220
B-But, even then...

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:17.580
Also, like I said earlier...

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:20.390
The more I eat, the more full I get.

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:23.090
Isn’t that a disadvantage for
Japan, who’s late finishing up?

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:26.110
If you still want me to, though, I’ll eat it.

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:30.410
Do we have your consent,
Japanese representative?

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:33.220
P-Playing dirty little tricks!

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:37.430
I guess they really did know what the second preliminary was going to be beforehand,

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:40.940
and made sure to get the
ingredients for last year’s winning bread...

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:43.320
Baldy.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:45.260
There’s no cause for worry.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:48.200
Even if they received a perfect score,

00:14:48.710 --> 00:14:50.950
I cannot be cut with a dirty sword.

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:52.630
Suwabara!

00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:53.700
Don’t call me Baldy!!

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:57.220
I do apologize.

00:14:57.220 --> 00:15:00.140
I got a perfect score ahead of you.

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:02.020
I’ll say it one more time...

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:03.790
The only one who’ll die is you!

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.510
Heh... Rude little fellow...

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:13.470
Sorry for the wait, Mr. Clown.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:15.980
Pain d'épice Kai

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:17.980
Eat.

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:21.120
I got tired of waiting.

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:22.600
All right, without any delay...

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:25.300
Chomp.

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:39.090
That was when I first
worked out the cloning technique...

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:43.520
Thanks to the cloning technique, the
performance in Japan was a huge success.

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:45.420
The performance ran for a very long time.

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:48.420
Drink up!

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:51.860
Thanks to you, Bolneze,
it’s a great success!

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:53.980
Yeah, Boss-to-be.

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:56.140
You’re truly great, Pierrot.

00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:59.390
You are, without doubt,
a legendary clown.

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:04.210
It’s weird having you praise me so much, Carn.

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:06.250
What was that you said?

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:11.130
Being acknowledged by everyone, I was in ecstasy.

00:16:11.590 --> 00:16:12.340
But...

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:13.700
Umm...

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:16.700
You’re Quedam’s...

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:18.340
Yeah.

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:21.020
Mr. Carn, who performs on the trapeze, right?

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:24.460
Yeah, that’s right.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.890
Oh, we were right!

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:27.730
You’re so cool!

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:28.890
Autograph, please!

00:16:28.890 --> 00:16:30.690
May we take a photograph with you?

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:38.220
The popular ones were always the
people on the trapeze and other showy acts.

00:16:38.950 --> 00:16:41.240
No matter how amazing a trick the clown shows,

00:16:41.240 --> 00:16:43.830
in the end, he plays the fool and falls.

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:46.230
He has to be uncool.

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:50.010
He can’t possibly be popular, can he?

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:53.710
It’s really an unpleasant role...

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:55.450
A clown...

00:16:55.840 --> 00:17:00.450
Moreover, if you’re without your makeup, no
one will even know that you’re Quedam’s clown.

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:02.700
Come to Maple.

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:04.920
Here you go.

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:13.920
Autograph, please!

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:16.860
O-On a pocket tissue?!

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:18.740
Or rather, you know who I am?

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:20.280
I don’t have my makeup on...

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:21.450
Of course I do!

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:23.070
I mean, yes, I do.

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:24.750
I’m a big fan...

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:27.660
I’ve been to your performance ten times now.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:28.940
Rather, I really like you.

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:32.650
Quedam’s Super Entertainer.

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:36.030
You’re Mr. Pierrot Bolneze, right?

00:17:36.520 --> 00:17:39.510
Her name was Kimura Megumi...

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:42.430
The only person who found me in Japan.

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:44.040
That’s what I thought.

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:47.310
In the twinkle of an eye, we fell in love.

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:50.540
Every night, after the circus was over, we’d talk.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:18:00.800
It was like... I’d been lonely, all by myself.

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:06.000
It’s all right now.

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:08.920
You’re no longer alone, right?

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:11.000
Then, one day...

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:12.020
What?!

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:14.110
We’re going to America next?

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:16.710
Yeah. It seems that our success in Japan

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:20.050
has reached the ears of the
higher-ups of television in America.

00:18:20.050 --> 00:18:22.090
You did it, Bolneze!

00:18:22.090 --> 00:18:24.120
Even David Mopperfield would be envious!

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.120
We’ll get to perform at the Mirage in Las Vegas!

00:18:28.050 --> 00:18:29.560
What’s wrong, Bolneze?

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:30.970
You’re not happy?

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:32.350
That’s not it...

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:36.270
After the performance in Las Vegas,
you’ll be both the clown and the boss.

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:37.640
I’ll leave things to you.

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:39.280
Very well.

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:44.990
Of course I was happy about
becoming the boss and going to Las Vegas.

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:47.580
But, in that case, Megu and I’d have to...

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:50.380
Hey, Megu...

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:55.710
Come with you to Las Vegas?

00:18:55.710 --> 00:18:56.840
Yeah.

00:18:58.380 --> 00:18:59.360
I can’t.

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:02.210
Why?

00:19:02.210 --> 00:19:03.720
I’m the boss now!

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:06.050
I can support one more person...

00:19:06.050 --> 00:19:08.890
Even I have my parents and my family.

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:12.080
I have customers waiting for my smile as well.

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:16.940
Also, I don’t speak any languages
other than Japanese and the Tochigi dialect.

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:18.470
I’d just be in your way.

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:20.110
That’s not true!

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:29.560
I knew that this day would come soon.

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:34.020
That’s why I’ve been carrying
something around for a long time.

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:39.590
Pretend that this is me, and keep it safe.

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:53.180
Why, Megu?

00:19:53.180 --> 00:19:55.540
Why didn’t you come with me?

00:19:56.060 --> 00:19:57.650
We loved each other so much...

00:19:58.650 --> 00:20:00.550
Women are full of mysteries.

00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:04.990
And, this gift that you gave me in the end...

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:07.560
It’s...

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:10.830
Nande Ebisu?

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:14.790
It’s an amazing bread!

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:15.950
Perfect score!

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:19.110
No, more than that,
Japanese representative!

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:22.110
He did it!

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:23.360
Yeah!

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:25.570
Of course.

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:27.630
But... somehow...

00:20:27.630 --> 00:20:30.800
the reaction this time was rather short, wasn’t it?

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:32.830
That’s not fair, Kawachi!

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:35.720
I would actually like to give you 7 points,

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:37.520
but the rules say that 5 points
is the maximum score, so...

00:20:37.520 --> 00:20:38.340
I’m sorry.

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:39.730
Don’t worry about it.

00:20:39.730 --> 00:20:42.050
It’s done so well that I think
even 10 points wouldn’t suffice.

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:44.730
To someone who can say something
as impudent as that without hesitation,

00:20:44.730 --> 00:20:46.740
I shall give you something to apologize for the 2 points.

00:20:51.030 --> 00:20:52.930
Nande Ebisu?

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:54.530
Oh, Megu...

00:20:54.530 --> 00:20:57.650
I’ve been carrying your
memory around for a long time, but...

00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:00.340
I will now forget you.

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:01.880
Thank you, Japanese representative.

00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:02.790
Why is it an Ebisu?

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:03.080
That pain d’épice
Why is it an Ebisu?

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:04.340
Yeah, I wonder why.
That pain d’épice

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:06.090
gave me the courage to try out a new romance.

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:08.660
But, it’s kinda cute...

00:21:09.420 --> 00:21:11.410
I cannot accept it.

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:13.550
Even if it’s a pain d’épice,

00:21:13.550 --> 00:21:18.170
with 34 ingredients added to it,
there’s no way that it could taste good.

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:22.230
Moreover, to think that you
actually evaluated it at 7 points...

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:24.510
It looks like you haven’t noticed.

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:30.320
That guy with the bandanna crushed all
the ingredients very finely with his fist.

00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:32.640
With great intensity.

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:40.150
So, that’s why it took so long?

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:42.860
Pain d'épice Kai
That was the “Kai” factor in my pain d’épice.

00:21:43.250 --> 00:21:45.110
That’s amazing, Suwabara!

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:48.380
By crushing the ingredients into fine particles,

00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:51.590
he created a completely new flavor.

00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:53.950
Since the ingredients had a
large number of fruits in them,

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:58.310
“Mixed Juice with Almonds and Nuts,
Giving It a Crisp Consistency, Spicy Bread,”

00:21:58.310 --> 00:21:59.500
is what you can call it.

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:04.780
It’s such a long name that I
can’t really think of it as delicious.

00:22:05.560 --> 00:22:08.230
However, Pierrot is a world-level judge.

00:22:08.230 --> 00:22:10.150
The taste must be the real thing.

00:22:10.150 --> 00:22:12.230
We have no choice but to accept it.

00:22:12.650 --> 00:22:15.040
By the way, Bandanna Boy...

00:22:15.410 --> 00:22:18.730
Your bread was really amazing, but...

00:22:19.490 --> 00:22:23.010
Next time, use a mixer
when making something like that.

00:22:23.580 --> 00:22:25.670
Crushing it with your fist must be hard, right?

00:22:25.670 --> 00:22:27.400
I’ll lend you one anytime.

00:22:29.550 --> 00:22:32.240
You should’ve said that earlier!

00:24:05.490 --> 00:24:07.070
You’ve passed the preliminaries.
Good work, Japan.

00:24:07.070 --> 00:24:08.320
The finals are next.

00:24:08.320 --> 00:24:10.950
Now, becoming #1 in the world
is really no longer just a dream.

00:24:10.950 --> 00:24:12.620
We can do it... We can do it!!

00:24:12.620 --> 00:24:14.700
You don’t know anything, do you?

00:24:14.700 --> 00:24:16.160
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.160 --> 00:24:17.390
The world pays attention!!

00:24:17.390 --> 00:24:18.920
The Monaco Cup finals begin!

00:24:18.920 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.550 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.730 --> 00:24:24.840
The pain d’épice that Suwabara made.

00:24:24.840 --> 00:24:26.590
Épice means “spice” in French.

00:24:26.590 --> 00:24:28.590
Its characterizing feature is the subtle flavor of spices.

00:24:28.590 --> 00:24:31.750
It’s the famed product of Dijon,
of the French province of Burgundy.

00:24:31.750 --> 00:24:34.230
Really?!
